       sector (e.g., pick one rotation index 0-3 and use it for most partial orbits).
    5. Place the square at a random valid position in the 10x10 grid (>=1 margin all sides).
    6. Write the retained pixels (full orbits + 1 pixel per partial orbit) onto a bg grid -> input.
    7. Verify solver recovers the intended output (unique smallest rotation-consistent square).
